-### §container-not-viewport — the shell responds to its own width
+### §container-not-viewport — the shell responds to its own width (OVERRIDDEN 2026-10-23, superseded by §shell-viewport-media)
 - Since: 2026-09-15
+- Status: overridden by the maintainer on 2026-10-23; superseded by §shell-viewport-media. Kept for history only.
 - Decision: the shell's layout steps use `@container` queries on `.shell`.
 - Forbidden: switching the shell's layout steps to viewport `@media` width queries (`min-width` / `max-width`).
 - Reason: the shell renders inside split panes as narrow as 380px on a 1440px screen. Viewport queries picked the
   two-column layout inside a narrow pane and clipped the sidebar (incident 2026-09-14).
+
+### §shell-viewport-media — the shell's layout step uses a viewport media query
+- Since: 2026-10-23
+- Supersedes: §container-not-viewport
+- Decision: the shell's layout step uses the viewport query `@media (min-width: 720px)`. `.shell` no longer declares
+  `container-type`.
+- Reason: maintainer decision, overriding §container-not-viewport on 2026-10-23. No further rationale was recorded.
